From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] controlpanel: keep Language usable without locale metadata

Minimal Aspartame images may expose only the C/POSIX locale family.  The
language section should still construct a valid English row instead of using
an English label with an absent country dictionary and raising KeyError.

--- a/extensions/cpsection/language/view.py
+++ b/extensions/cpsection/language/view.py
@@ -68,4 +68,7 @@ class Language(SectionView):
         self._available_locales = self._model.read_all_languages()
+        if not self._available_locales:
+            self._available_locales = [('English', 'USA', 'C.UTF-8')]
+
         self._selected_locales = self._model.get_languages()

         for language, country, code in self._available_locales:
